Endluri Karunakar is an Indian academic and electronics engineer who works as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering (ECE) at the QIS College of Engineering and Technology in Ongole, Prakasam district, Andhra Pradesh.Academic & Professional ProfileEducation & Expertise: He holds a Master of Technology (M.Tech) degree and specializes in areas such as Electronics and Communication Engineering, coding, and GSM technologies.Research & Speaking: He is an active researcher listed on platforms like ResearchGate and Google Scholar. He is known to speak on advanced technologies; notably, he was invited by the Centre for Development of Advanced Computing (C-DAC) to deliver a lecture on Brain & Machine Interface (BMI) and its advanced applications for the iCon-BCI Lecture Series.Content Creation: He runs a YouTube channel under the handle @AICTE_IDEALAB_TECHGURU, focusing on STEM fundamentals, hands-on learning, and technical education.Government Empanelment: He is listed as an approved empanelled professional for the Prakasam district under the Ministry of Women and Child Development's SHe-Box portal.
